@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.3103 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [967 x i8] }> <{ [967 x i8] c"# `string_deref_patterns`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#87121]\0A\0A[#87121]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/87121\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThis feature permits pattern matching `String` to `&str` through [its `Deref` implementation].\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(string_deref_patterns)]\0A\0Apub enum Value {\0A    String(String),\0A    Number(u32),\0A}\0A\0Apub fn is_it_the_answer(value: Value) -> bool {\0A    match value {\0A        Value::String(\2242\22) => true,\0A        Value::Number(42) => true,\0A        _ => false,\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0AWithout this feature other constructs such as match guards have to be used.\0A\0A```rust\0A# pub enum Value {\0A#    String(String),\0A#    Number(u32),\0A# }\0A#\0Apub fn is_it_the_answer(value: Value) -> bool {\0A    match value {\0A        Value::String(s) if s == \2242\22 => true,\0A        Value::Number(42) => true,\0A        _ => false,\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0A[its `Deref` implementation]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/string/struct.String.html#impl-Deref-for-String\0A" }>, align 1
